<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<!--
	Global gatekeeper content and appearance, used by the script.teleport.GlobalGatekeeper script.

	Everything the player sees is defined here. The behavior and the economy (rows per page, teleport
	delay, popular tab limits, default prices and the whole dynamic pricing formula) live server side,
	on config/mods/gatekeeper.properties.

	<layout>
		Sizes of the generated tables. The header row and the list rows are generated out of the very
		same <column> nodes, which is what keeps them aligned - never describe a header on a HTM.

		width       : width, in pixels, of every generated table (tab bar, header, rows, page selector).
		              Fed to the HTMs as %width%. Keep it below 290, so the scrollbar doesn't eat the
		              last column.
		rowHeight   : height, in pixels, of a single row of a list. Rows never wrap (see maxChars), so
		              every row of every page owns that exact height.
		headerHeight: height, in pixels, of the header row of a list.
		tabHeight   : height, in pixels, of a row of the tab bar.
		tabColumns  : maximum amount of tabs shown on a single row of the tab bar. Above it, the tabs
		              are spread on multiple rows, so their labels stay readable.
		maxPages    : maximum amount of page links shown by the page selector, centered on the current
		              page. The selector always stays on a single line.
		ellipsis    : suffix appended to a shortened cell content.
		pageHeight  : total height, in pixels, every page is padded up to - the tab bar, the "overhead"
		              of the page and its list rows included. Since it is the very same on every page,
		              the page selector always lands on the same spot ; and since it is set slightly
		              above the height of the dialog, the scrollbar stays shown everywhere. 0 disables
		              the padding. Raise it until the scrollbar shows up on every tab, no more.

		<table id="areas">   : columns of the areas list page. Ids : name, price, capital.
		<table id="mixed">   : same page, used by the tab mixing areas and direct points - it shows a
		                      level where "areas" shows a capital. Ids : name, price, lvl.
		<table id="points">  : columns of the teleport points list page. Ids : name, price, lvl.
		<table id="popular"> : columns of the most used points page. Ids : name, price, lvl.

		Those four ids are the defaults ; a tab picks any other <table> through its "table" attribute,
		which is how two tabs of the same kind can own different columns. Add as many tables as needed.
		That attribute describes the list the tab itself generates : the sub lists opened from an areas
		tab are pages of their own, and always use the "points" table.

		Column ids the script knows, whatever the page :
		  name    : the destination, itself the teleport link (or the link opening the sub list).
		  price   : the price to pay.
		  capital : on an areas row, the "capital" shortcut of the area ; on a direct row without any
		            capital of its own, its level ; on a points row, the level.
		  lvl     : the monster level. A row leading to a sub list shows the "locked" label instead,
		            since a whole area owns no level of its own.
		An unknown id renders an empty cell, and the columns are drawn in the order they are written.

		overhead : height, in pixels, everything but the tab bar and the list rows takes on the HTM of
		           that page - separators, headline, header row and the %footer% row. Substracted from
		           pageHeight to know how much the list has to be padded with. Only worth touching after
		           editing the HTM of the page. Rough guide : <br> 16, <br1> 8, a separator img 1,
		           a header or footer row 18. The optional intro of a tab is counted apart, see the
		           "introHeight" attribute of <item>.

		The %footer% row holds the back link on the left and the page selector on the right, and sits
		right under the list. It is always emitted, even when both are empty, so that every page keeps
		the very same height. %filler% comes after it, and fills whatever is left down to pageHeight.

		<column>
			id      : the column the script feeds ; an unknown id is simply ignored.
			header  : caption shown on the header row. Empty generates an empty header cell.
			width   : width, in pixels. The columns of a table must sum up to the layout width.
			maxChars: amount of characters above which the content is shortened, on the last word
			          boundary when possible. 0 never shortens - and lets a long name wrap, which makes
			          its row taller than the others. Roughly width / 6.
			align   : left, center or right.

	<colors>
		Every color of the dialog. An empty value keeps the client default : a transparent background
		for a row, a plain white text for a label.

		row / altRow  : background of the odd / even rows of the lists.
		header        : background of the header row of the lists.
		headerText    : text of the header row of the lists.
		title         : headline of the pages, fed to the HTMs as %titleColor%.
		tabBar        : background of the tab bar.
		tab           : default color of a tab, overridden by the "color" attribute of a given <item>.
		activeTab     : color of the currently shown tab.
		name          : name column of the lists.
		point         : sub-point part of a name - the " - Center" of "Cruma Marshlands - Center".
		price         : price column of the lists.
		free          : price column, when the teleport is free.
		disabled      : everything out of reach - locked points, unreachable capitals, empty lists.
		page / activePage : page selector links, and the current page.
		level         : monster level shown on the "lvl" column of the lists, and on the third column of
		                a direct row of the areas list.

	<labels>
		Every generated text of the dialog. The static texts live on the HTMs of
		data/html/script/teleport/GlobalGatekeeper.

		noble    : label shown on the "lvl" column, when the point requires noblesse.
		locked   : label shown on the "lvl" column, when the point is out of reach, or when its monster
		           levels are unset. It also fills the third column of the areas list, on a row leading
		           to a sub list without any "capital" shortcut - a whole area owns no level of its own.
		free     : label shown on the price column, when the teleport is free.
		empty    : label shown instead of an empty list.
		back     : label of the link leading back to the areas list, shown on the left of the footer row.
		prevPage / nextPage : labels of the page selector arrows, shown on the right of the footer row.
		popupSeparator    : written between the destination and its price, on the confirmation box
		                    shown before a teleport. Beware, a double dash can't be written inside
		                    this very comment, but it is perfectly fine inside an attribute.
		currencyChars     : amount of characters kept of the currency name, next to a price. 0 shows the
		                    whole name, localized by the client ("57 000 Adena"). 1 shows "57 000 A".
		currencyLowerCase : true lowercases the shortened currency name ("57 000 a").

		Angle brackets are safe here : write them as &lt; / &gt;, the script feeds them back to the
		client escaped, so a "&lt;&lt; back" label doesn't get read as a tag and swallowed.

	<npc>
		id / menu : binds a npc id to a menu id. Add a line to make any npc a gatekeeper.

	<menu>
		Holds the tabs of the dialog. Multiple npcs can share a menu. priceId / price / noblePrice
		can be set on <menu>, <item>, <area> and <loc> - the closest definition wins, the default being
		the one of config/mods/gatekeeper.properties.
		Beware : setting price on a <menu>, <item> or <area> gives that very same fixed price to every
		point below it, which disables the pricing formula for all of them. Leave it unset (-1) to
		let each point be priced on its own distance.

	<item> (a tab of the top bar)
		- holding <area> nodes    : generates the areas list page (areas.htm). A <loc> written next to
		                            the areas becomes a row teleporting right away, instead of leading
		                            to a sub list - so both kinds can be freely mixed, in the order
		                            they are written. On such a direct row, the name itself is the
		                            teleport link and the third column shows its monster level ; on a
		                            regular row leading to a sub list, that column shows the "capital"
		                            shortcut when set, or the "locked" label of <labels> otherwise.
		- holding <loc> nodes only: generates the points list page (locations.htm), without any area.
		- type="popular"          : generates the most used points page (popular.htm).
		- page="somefile.htm"     : shows an additional datapack HTM of the script folder.
		- bypass="..."            : any regular bypass, handled by the core (multisell, quest, ...).
		name / color              : label and color of the tab, the default color being the "tab" one of
		                            <colors>. %objectId% is supported on bypasses.
		table                     : id of the <table> of <layout> used to render the list of this tab.
		                            Unset uses the default one of the kind of tab : "areas", "points"
		                            or "popular". The sub lists of an areas tab always use "points".
		intro / introHeight       : optional HTM fragment of the script folder, shown above the tab bar
		                            of the areas list page, and its height in pixels. Since the script
		                            can't measure a text on its own, that height is what keeps the page
		                            as tall as the tabs without an intro. Drop both attributes and the
		                            tab simply shows no intro at all.
		Tabs are spread on multiple rows above "tabColumns" entries, so their labels stay readable.

	<loc>
		id       : unique id, used as database key of the teleport counter. Never reuse it.
		name     : location name, shown on the name column, itself the teleport link.
		point    : optional sub-point name, appended to the name after a " - " and colored apart.
		type     : STANDARD or NOBLE (requires a noblesse player).
		lvl      : optional, monster level(s) roaming this spot, shown on the "lvl" column of the teleport
		           points list - and on the third column of the areas list, when the point is written as
		           a direct row. Either a single value ("47") or a range ("20-25"). Unset shows the
		           "locked" label of <labels> instead - most often true of a real city or a village.
		x / y / z: destination.
		castleId : optional, forbids the teleport while the castle siege is in progress.
		minLevel / maxLevel : optional level restriction.
		price    : optional. -1 (default) lets the pricing formula compute it, 0 makes it free, any other value is a fixed base price.
-->
<list>
	<layout width="280" rowHeight="18" headerHeight="18" tabHeight="18" tabColumns="4" maxPages="10" pageHeight="390" ellipsis="...">
		<table id="areas" overhead="104">
			<column id="name" header="Destination" width="160" maxChars="22" align="left" />
			<column id="price" header="Price" width="60" maxChars="0" align="left" />
			<column id="capital" header="Capital" width="60" maxChars="14" align="left" />
		</table>
		<table id="mixed" overhead="104">
			<column id="name" header="Destination" width="175" maxChars="25" align="left" />
			<column id="price" header="Price" width="60" maxChars="0" align="left" />
			<column id="lvl" header="Level" width="50" maxChars="0" align="center" />
		</table>
		<table id="points" overhead="96">
			<column id="name" header="Location" width="175" maxChars="35" align="left" />
			<column id="price" header="Price" width="60" maxChars="0" align="left" />
			<column id="lvl" header="Level" width="50" maxChars="0" align="center" />
		</table>
		<table id="popular" overhead="96">
			<column id="name" header="Location" width="175" maxChars="25" align="left" />
			<column id="price" header="Price" width="60" maxChars="0" align="left" />
			<column id="lvl" header="Level" width="50" maxChars="0" align="center" />
		</table>
	</layout>

	<colors row="000000" altRow="" header="000000" headerText="9F9F9F" title="8F8F8F" tabBar="000000" tab="FFFFFF" activeTab="LEVEL" name="" point="8F8F8F" price="LEVEL" free="00FF00" disabled="707070" page="" activePage="LEVEL" level="FFFFFF" />

